1
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:06,096
This one is pure red rock canyon country!

2
00:00:06,096 --> 00:00:11,084
A four-hundred-fifty-foot sandstone tower standing all by itself.

3
00:00:11,084 --> 00:00:14,077
Canyon drop-offs right beside the road.

4
00:00:14,077 --> 00:00:17,300
And desert bighorn sheep just hanging out!

5
00:00:18,250 --> 00:00:27,289
This is Colorado National Monument: Rim Rock Drive, 23 miles right along the edge of the canyons, between Fruita and Grand Junction.

6
00:00:27,289 --> 00:00:30,850
Stick around till the end for the full trip planner!

7
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:32,906
Here's the plan!

8
00:00:32,906 --> 00:00:43,340
We leave Fruita, climb up to the Saddlehorn visitor center, see Independence Monument, peek over Cold Shivers Point, and roll down into Grand Junction!

9
00:00:44,290 --> 00:00:48,285
We're starting in Fruita, right at the foot of the canyons!

10
00:00:48,285 --> 00:00:53,904
This area is famous for dinosaur fossils, so check out the dinosaur museum in town.

11
00:00:53,904 --> 00:00:54,920
Okay, up we go!

12
00:00:55,870 --> 00:01:02,171
Right away, the road switchbacks straight up the cliffs, through tunnels carved in the rock!

13
00:01:02,171 --> 00:01:05,047
Much of it was built by hand in the 1930s.

14
00:01:05,047 --> 00:01:07,650
Watch for Balanced Rock on the way up!

15
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:12,570
This is the Saddlehorn visitor center, perched right on the rim!

16
00:01:12,570 --> 00:01:18,340
Keep your eyes peeled, because desert bighorn sheep love to wander onto the road around here!

17
00:01:19,290 --> 00:01:25,370
Just down the rim, and here comes the most famous view in the whole monument!

18
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:33,261
That's Independence Monument, a four-hundred-fifty-foot sandstone tower standing all by itself!

19
00:01:33,261 --> 00:01:40,640
John Otto, the man who fought to create this park, climbed it back in 1911 and planted a flag on top!

20
00:01:41,590 --> 00:01:49,500
Now we follow the rim, past Artists Point and up onto the high mesa, way above the valley floor!

21
00:01:50,450 --> 00:01:52,523
Welcome to Cold Shivers Point!

22
00:01:52,523 --> 00:01:55,771
Walk out to the railing and peek over the edge.

23
00:01:55,771 --> 00:01:58,397
Yep, that's where the name comes from.

24
00:01:58,397 --> 00:01:58,950
Shivers!

25
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:03,854
Down the switchbacks on the east side and into Grand Junction!

26
00:02:03,854 --> 00:02:07,490
The valley down below is famous for peaches and wineries.

27
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:14,290
Welcome to Grand Junction, named for the spot where the Colorado and Gunnison Rivers meet.

28
00:02:14,290 --> 00:02:17,735
Head out to nearby Palisade for wineries and peaches.

29
00:02:17,735 --> 00:02:18,450
What a day!

30
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:20,887
And that's the drive!

31
00:02:20,887 --> 00:02:28,180
29 miles from Fruita to Grand Junction, with 23 of them on Rim Rock Drive, right along the canyon rims.

32
00:02:29,130 --> 00:02:32,290
Here's your trip planner, everything in one place.

33
00:02:32,290 --> 00:02:34,060
Pause and grab a screenshot!

34
00:02:37,630 --> 00:02:39,285
Thanks for riding along!

35
00:02:39,285 --> 00:02:45,630
Hit subscribe, and next time we're heading south to the tallest sand dunes in North America!
